❓Question
Given two strings ransomNote and magazine, return true if ransomNote can be constructed using the letters from magazine.
Each letter from magazine can only be used once.

Example
Input: ransomNote = "a"
       magazine = "b"
Output: false

✅Approach
Create a HashMap to store the frequency of characters in magazine.
Traverse magazine and count every character.
Traverse ransomNote.
For each character, check how many are available in the map.
If the count is 0, return false.
Otherwise, use one occurrence by decreasing its count by 1.
If we successfully process the whole ransomNote, return true.

Code
class Solution {
    public boolean canConstruct(String ransomNote, String magazine) {
        HashMap<Character, Integer> mapM = new HashMap<>();
        if(ransomNote.length() > magazine.length()){
            return false;
        }
        for(int i = 0; i < magazine.length(); i++){
            char chM = magazine.charAt(i);
            mapM.put(chM, mapM.getOrDefault(chM, 0) + 1);
        }
        for(int i = 0; i < ransomNote.length(); i++){
            char ch = ransomNote.charAt(i);
            int currentcounts = mapM.getOrDefault(ch, 0);
            if(currentcounts == 0){
                return false;
            }
            mapM.put(ch, currentcounts - 1);
        }
        return true;
    }
}

Time Complexity
O(n + m)
Space Complexity
O(n)
